# Response headers for the static assets (Workers reads this from dist/; it does
# not apply to responses the Worker itself builds, i.e. /api/*).
#
# Cross-origin isolation, so the Python runner can share an interrupt buffer
# with its worker: Stop and the time limits end a run without reloading the
# interpreter. The app loads nothing from another origin, so require-corp
# blocks nothing. vite.config.ts sends the same pair in dev and preview.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

# The interpreter lives under its version number, so a given path never
# changes content: cache it for good, and the 13 MB moves once per release.
/pyodide/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
